{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":242683,"duration_api_ms":240561,"num_turns":18,"result":"Perfect! I have successfully produced the WDD (Workflow Definition Document) YAML file for the 1000Genome workflow. Here's the complete file:\n\n```yaml\nschema_version: wrd-7.0\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: wrd:1000genome\n  workflow_name: 1000genome\n  version: 1\n  created_by: claude\n  created_date: 2026-03-11\n  description: >\n    The 1000 Genomes workflow processes genomic variation data from the 1000 Genomes Project\n    to identify mutational overlaps and perform statistical analyses. It fetches and parses\n    VCF phase3 data by chromosome, computes SIFT mutation effect predictions, measures\n    overlaps in mutations between individual pairs stratified by population, and generates\n    frequency distributions via random sampling.\n  generated_by: static_analysis\n  notes: Analysis from Pegasus workflow definition (daxgen.py) and task implementations.\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  overall_pattern: acyclic_dag_multi_dataset_fanout\n  pattern_notes: >\n    Chromosome-level parallelism with independent per-chromosome processing.\n    Individuals processing parallelized per chromosome via chunking (ind_jobs).\n    Wide fan-out from sifting+individuals to paired mutation_overlap/frequency jobs\n    (one job per population, 6+ populations). Aggregation in individuals_merge.\n  estimated_stages: 3\n  estimated_tasks: 7\n  integrity_hash: unknown\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: stage:fetch_parse\n    stage_name: Fetch and Parse\n    description: >\n      Extracts SNP variant data from 1000 Genomes Phase3 VCF files and parses\n      individual-level genotype information. Can be parallelized per chromosome\n      and further split into multiple individuals jobs per chromosome (chunked by line ranges).\n    tasks:\n      - task:individuals\n\n  - stage_id: stage:sift_prediction\n    description: >\n      Computes SIFT (Sorting Intolerant From Tolerant) scores for SNP variants\n      using Variant Effect Predictor (VEP) annotations. Filters variants to keep\n      only those with SIFT predictions and rs numbers.\n    tasks:\n      - task:sifting\n\n  - stage_id: stage:merge_individuals\n    description: >\n      Aggregates individual-level mutation data from chunked parallel jobs\n      (if ind_jobs > 1) into a single per-chromosome tarball.\n    tasks:\n      - task:individuals_merge\n\n  - stage_id: stage:analysis\n    description: >\n      Performs population-stratified pairwise mutation overlap analysis\n      and random frequency sampling analysis. Generates numerical results and plots.\n    tasks:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: task:individuals\n    task_name: individuals\n    description: >\n      Extracts SNP genotype data from Phase3 VCF file for a chromosome.\n      Processes lines [counter, stop) and outputs individual-level files\n      (one file per individual with that individual's mutations).\n      Outputs are compressed into a tar.gz for efficient staging.\n    implementation: bin/individuals.py\n    executable_type: python3_script\n    language: python\n    io_access_type: posix_independent\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    task_class: data_transformation\n    inputs:\n      - data:vcf_chromosome\n      - data:columns_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:individuals_chunk_tarball\n    input_multiplicity: 1_to_n_per_chromosome\n    output_cardinality: one_per_job\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Heavy memory usage due to large VCF parsing (250k lines per chromosome).\n      Writes many small files (one per individual, typically ~2500 per run).\n      Decompresses implicitly during processing. Memory requirement scales with\n      chunk size (input_lines / ind_jobs). Small-file I/O overhead is significant;\n      mitigated by tar.gz compression at job output.\n    io_dominance: text_read_heavy\n    dependencies: []\n\n  - task_id: task:individuals_merge\n    task_name: individuals_merge\n    description: >\n      Aggregates multiple individuals job outputs (tar.gz files)\n      from parallel chunked processing into a single merged tarball\n      per chromosome. Used when ind_jobs > 1; otherwise is a pass-through.\n      Decompresses each input tarball, concatenates file contents by individual,\n      then recompresses.\n    implementation: bin/individuals_merge.py\n    executable_type: python3_script\n    language: python\n    io_access_type: posix_independent\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    task_class: data_aggregation\n    inputs:\n      - data:individuals_chunk_tarball\n    outputs:\n      - data:individuals_merged_tarball\n    input_multiplicity: n_to_1_per_chromosome\n    output_cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Extracts tar.gz files, reads individual files, concatenates by name,\n      writes merged files to disk, then recompresses. Temporary extraction\n      overhead. Ratio of extract/compress to pure I/O is high (~30% processing).\n    io_dominance: tarball_read_write_heavy\n    dependencies:\n      - pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\n\n  - task_id: task:sifting\n    task_name: sifting\n    description: >\n      Filters VEP (Variant Effect Predictor) annotations to extract SNPs\n      with SIFT scores. Reads VEP file, greps for deleterious/tolerated SIFT\n      predictions, extracts line numbers, rs IDs, ENSG IDs, SIFT scores,\n      and phenotype predictions. Outputs a single text file per chromosome.\n    implementation: bin/sifting.py\n    executable_type: python3_script\n    language: python\n    io_access_type: posix_independent\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    task_class: data_filtering\n    inputs:\n      - data:vep_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:sifted_file\n    input_multiplicity: 1_to_1_per_chromosome\n    output_cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Uses shell grep via subprocess for filtering (subprocess.run with grep).\n      Regex-based field extraction on VEP columns. Creates intermediate temp file.\n      Moderate text processing overhead. Typical output is 10-20% of input size.\n    io_dominance: text_read_write_moderate\n    dependencies: []\n\n  - task_id: task:mutation_overlap\n    task_name: mutation_overlap\n    description: >\n      Measures pairwise mutation overlap between individuals in a population\n      for a chromosome. Reads merged individuals tarball, SIFT scores, population list,\n      and columns file. Computes overlap matrices, generates numerical result files\n      and plots. Outputs tar.gz archive containing results and visualizations.\n    implementation: bin/mutation_overlap.py\n    executable_type: python3_script\n    language: python\n    io_access_type: posix_independent\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    task_class: analysis\n    inputs:\n      - data:individuals_merged_tarball\n      - data:sifted_file\n      - data:population_file\n      - data:columns_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:mutation_overlap_archive\n    input_multiplicity: 1_to_n_per_population\n    output_cardinality: one_per_chromosome_population\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Extracts tar.gz input, reads population file, reads per-individual mutation files,\n      computes pairwise overlap as Counter objects. Generates multiple output files\n      and plots using matplotlib (PNG). High numpy array manipulation. Moderate memory\n      for overlap matrices (O(n^2) individuals). Creates output directory structure.\n    io_dominance: tarball_read_heavy_plotting_heavy\n    dependencies:\n      - pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n      - pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n\n  - task_id: task:frequency\n    task_name: frequency\n    description: >\n      Performs random sampling of mutation frequencies within a population.\n      Selects random individuals (n_indiv=52 pairs) repeatedly (n_runs=1000)\n      and computes overlap distributions without SIFT filtering. Reads same inputs\n      as mutation_overlap but applies random sampling strategy. Outputs numerical\n      results and plots.\n    implementation: bin/frequency.py\n    executable_type: python3_script\n    language: python\n    io_access_type: posix_independent\n    restart_model: idempotent\n    task_class: analysis\n    inputs:\n      - data:individuals_merged_tarball\n      - data:sifted_file\n      - data:population_file\n      - data:columns_file\n    outputs:\n      - data:frequency_archive\n    input_multiplicity: 1_to_n_per_population\n    output_cardinality: one_per_chromosome_population\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Similar to mutation_overlap but with random sampling loop (1000 runs).\n      Reads per-individual files repeatedly (statistical sampling). High CPU usage\n      for random generation and Counter operations. Memory for storing all permutation\n      results in memory before output. Generates plots for distributions.\n    io_dominance: tarball_read_heavy_plotting_heavy\n    dependencies:\n      - pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\n      - pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: data:vcf_chromosome\n    data_name: VCF Chromosome File\n    format: vcf\n    description: >\n      1000 Genomes Phase3 VCF file for a single chromosome. Contains SNP variant calls\n      for 2504 individuals. File naming: ALL.chrN.250000.vcf where N is chromosome number\n      and 250000 is typical line count.\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    cardinality_source: 22 chromosomes fixed\n    produced_by: null\n    consumed_by: [task:individuals]\n    lifecycle: input_root_data\n    format_hints: vcf_text_tabular_9plus_columns\n    size_estimate: gigabytes_scale\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_once_per_job\n    notes: Decompressed in memory during processing. Not a true input (comes from external source).\n\n  - data_id: data:individuals_chunk_tarball\n    data_name: Individuals Chunk Tarball\n    format: tar.gz\n    description: >\n      Compressed tarball containing individual-level mutation files from a single\n      individuals job (processing lines [counter, stop) of a chromosome).\n      Contains one text file per individual in the target population.\n      Naming: chrXn-<start>-<stop>.tar.gz\n    cardinality: many_per_chromosome_if_ind_jobs_gt_1\n    cardinality_source: (total_lines / ind_jobs) jobs per chromosome\n    produced_by: task:individuals\n    consumed_by: [task:individuals_merge]\n    lifecycle: intermediate_staging\n    format_hints: tar_gzip_text_files_nested\n    size_estimate: hundreds_of_megabytes\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_once_in_merge\n    notes: >\n      Intermediate artifact. Only produced if ind_jobs > 1. Enables horizontal scaling\n      of individuals job. Small-file I/O overhead mitigated by compression.\n\n  - data_id: data:individuals_merged_tarball\n    data_name: Individuals Merged Tarball\n    format: tar.gz\n    description: >\n      Final merged and compressed tarball containing individual-level mutation files\n      for all 2500+ individuals in a chromosome. One text file per individual.\n      Naming: chrXn.tar.gz\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    cardinality_source: one per chromosome\n    produced_by: task:individuals_merge\n    consumed_by: [task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    lifecycle: intermediate_primary\n    format_hints: tar_gzip_text_files_nested_large\n    size_estimate: multiple_gigabytes\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_by_two_tasks_per_chromosome\n    notes: >\n      Central data object. Reused by both mutation_overlap and frequency jobs\n      for each population. High-volume intermediate. Enables reuse across analysis tasks.\n\n  - data_id: data:vep_file\n    data_name: VEP Annotation File\n    format: vcf\n    description: >\n      Variant Effect Predictor (VEP) annotated VCF file for a chromosome.\n      Contains SIFT predictions in column 8 (INFO field).\n      Naming: typically chr<N>_sift_predictions.vcf or similar.\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    cardinality_source: 22 chromosomes fixed\n    produced_by: null\n    consumed_by: [task:sifting]\n    lifecycle: input_root_data\n    format_hints: vcf_text_with_sift_annotations\n    size_estimate: gigabytes_scale\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_once\n    notes: >\n      VEP-processed annotations. Stored in data/20130502/sifting/ directory.\n      Contains deleterious/tolerated SIFT predictions for filtering.\n\n  - data_id: data:sifted_file\n    data_name: Sifted SIFT File\n    format: text\n    description: >\n      Filtered SIFT scores for SNPs in a chromosome. Contains columns:\n      line_number, rs_id, ensg_id, sift_score, phenotype.\n      Naming: sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    cardinality_source: one per chromosome\n    produced_by: task:sifting\n    consumed_by: [task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    lifecycle: intermediate_primary\n    format_hints: text_tabular_5_columns_whitespace_delimited\n    size_estimate: hundreds_of_megabytes\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_by_two_tasks\n    notes: >\n      Central filtering output. Reused by both analysis tasks. Filters VEP predictions\n      to SIFT-annotated variants. Used to filter mutation lists during analysis.\n\n  - data_id: data:population_file\n    data_name: Population File\n    format: text\n    description: >\n      Whitespace-delimited file listing individual IDs in a population.\n      One ID per line. Examples: ALL, EUR, EAS, AFR, AMR, SAS, GBR.\n    cardinality: many_populations\n    cardinality_source: 7 fixed populations (1 ALL + 6 super-populations)\n    produced_by: null\n    consumed_by: [task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    lifecycle: input_root_data\n    format_hints: text_list_individual_ids\n    size_estimate: kilobytes_scale\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_by_two_tasks_per_population\n    notes: >\n      Static reference data. Stored in data/populations/ directory.\n      Defines which individuals belong to each analysis population.\n\n  - data_id: data:columns_file\n    data_name: Columns File\n    format: text\n    description: >\n      Whitespace-delimited file listing all individual IDs in order.\n      Used as master reference to map population IDs to per-individual file names.\n      Typically: columns.txt\n    cardinality: one_global\n    cardinality_source: fixed single file\n    produced_by: null\n    consumed_by: [task:individuals, task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    lifecycle: input_root_data\n    format_hints: text_list_individual_ids_ordered\n    size_estimate: kilobytes_scale\n    reuse_pattern: consumed_by_three_tasks\n    notes: >\n      Static metadata. ~2500 individual IDs. Used to map individual names to\n      per-individual mutation file names and population filtering.\n\n  - data_id: data:mutation_overlap_archive\n    data_name: Mutation Overlap Archive\n    format: tar.gz\n    description: >\n      Results archive containing mutation overlap matrices, statistics, and plots\n      for a chromosome in a population. Contains subdirectories: output_no_sift/\n      (numerical results) and plots_no_sift/ (PNG visualizations).\n      Naming: chrX-<population>.tar.gz\n    cardinality: many_per_population\n    cardinality_source: 22 chromosomes × 7 populations = 154 archives\n    produced_by: task:mutation_overlap\n    consumed_by: null\n    lifecycle: output_final\n    format_hints: tar_gzip_mixed_text_images\n    size_estimate: tens_to_hundreds_megabytes_per_archive\n    reuse_pattern: output_only\n    notes: >\n      Final output. Contains:\n      - total_mutations_individual.txt\n      - map_variations.txt\n      - mutation_index_array.txt\n      - individual_half_pairs_overlap.txt\n      - total_individual_pairs_overlap.txt\n      - random_mutations_individual_run_N.txt\n      - PNG plots (distribution, colormap, etc.)\n\n  - data_id: data:frequency_archive\n    data_name: Frequency Archive\n    format: tar.gz\n    description: >\n      Results archive containing frequency distribution results and plots\n      from random sampling analysis for a chromosome in a population.\n      Similar structure to mutation_overlap_archive.\n      Naming: chrX-<population>-freq.tar.gz\n    cardinality: many_per_population\n    cardinality_source: 22 chromosomes × 7 populations = 154 archives\n    produced_by: task:frequency\n    consumed_by: null\n    lifecycle: output_final\n    format_hints: tar_gzip_mixed_text_images\n    size_estimate: tens_to_hundreds_megabytes_per_archive\n    reuse_pattern: output_only\n    notes: >\n      Final output. Contains:\n      - total_mutations_individual_run_N.txt\n      - random_mutations_individual_run_N.txt\n      - PNG plots of frequency distributions and colormaps\n      - Statistical summaries per random run (1000 runs)\n\npc_edges:\n  - pc_id: pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\n    source_task: task:individuals\n    target_task: task:individuals_merge\n    data_object: data:individuals_chunk_tarball\n    pc_pattern: n_to_1_aggregation\n    cardinality_rule: >\n      All individuals jobs producing chunk tarballs for a chromosome feed\n      into single individuals_merge job for that chromosome.\n    temporal_order: individuals jobs complete before individuals_merge starts\n    notes: >\n      Aggregation point. Only materialized if ind_jobs > 1.\n      If ind_jobs == 1, this edge is bypassed and individuals output goes\n      directly to analysis tasks.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    source_task: task:individuals_merge\n    target_task: task:mutation_overlap\n    data_object: data:individuals_merged_tarball\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n_fan_out\n    cardinality_rule: >\n      Single merged chromosome data is consumed by one mutation_overlap job\n      per population (7 jobs per chromosome: 1 ALL + 6 super-populations).\n    temporal_order: individuals_merge completes before mutation_overlap jobs start\n    notes: >\n      Wide fan-out. Same tarball input to 7 parallel jobs per chromosome.\n      Enables population-stratified analysis without duplication.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\n    source_task: task:individuals_merge\n    target_task: task:frequency\n    data_object: data:individuals_merged_tarball\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n_fan_out\n    cardinality_rule: >\n      Single merged chromosome data consumed by one frequency job\n      per population (7 jobs per chromosome).\n    temporal_order: individuals_merge completes before frequency jobs start\n    notes: >\n      Wide fan-out, same as mutation_overlap. Both jobs read the same tarball\n      per population, enabling comparison of overlap vs. frequency results.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    source_task: task:sifting\n    target_object: data:sifted_file\n    target_task: task:mutation_overlap\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n_broadcast\n    cardinality_rule: >\n      Single sifted file per chromosome is used by all 7 mutation_overlap jobs\n      (one per population).\n    temporal_order: sifting completes before mutation_overlap jobs start\n    notes: >\n      Broadcast of filtering metadata. Same SIFT scores used across all\n      population-stratified overlap jobs.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\n    source_task: task:sifting\n    target_task: task:frequency\n    data_object: data:sifted_file\n    pc_pattern: 1_to_n_broadcast\n    cardinality_rule: >\n      Single sifted file per chromosome is used by all 7 frequency jobs.\n    temporal_order: sifting completes before frequency jobs start\n    notes: >\n      Broadcast of filtering metadata. Same SIFT scores used for filtering\n      during frequency analysis.\n\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_id: default\n    profile_name: Default Profile\n    description: >\n      Standard execution profile with default parameters.\n      Single individuals job per chromosome (ind_jobs=1).\n      All 22 chromosomes processed independently in parallel.\n      All 7 populations analyzed per chromosome.\n    required_task_ids:\n      - task:individuals\n      - task:individuals_merge\n      - task:sifting\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n    optional_task_ids: []\n    conditional_inclusions: []\n    parameters:\n      - param_id: param:ind_jobs\n        default_value: 1\n        description: >\n          Number of individuals jobs per chromosome.\n          If > 1, individuals output is aggregated by individuals_merge.\n          Must divide 250000 (typical lines per chromosome file).\n        valid_range: [1, 250]\n        notes: Affects parallelism and memory per job\n\n      - param_id: param:num_chromosomes\n        default_value: 22\n        description: Chromosomes to process (1-22)\n        valid_range: [1, 22]\n        notes: Typically all 22 for full analysis\n\n      - param_id: param:populations\n        default_value: [ALL, EUR, EAS, AFR, AMR, SAS, GBR]\n        description: Populations to analyze\n        valid_range: subset of [ALL, EUR, EAS, AFR, AMR, SAS, GBR]\n        notes: Each population generates separate analysis results\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  - pattern_type: per_chromosome_parallelism\n    description: >\n      Workflow processes each chromosome independently. No inter-chromosome\n      dependencies. All chromosomes can be processed in parallel.\n    evidence: Task definitions read chromosome-specific input/output filenames.\n\n  - pattern_type: per_population_analysis\n    description: >\n      Analysis tasks (mutation_overlap, frequency) are stratified by population.\n      Same data processed separately for each population.\n    evidence: Tasks take population_file as input, generate per-population outputs.\n\n  - pattern_type: horizontal_scaling_via_chunking\n    description: >\n      Individuals job can be horizontally scaled by chunking lines via ind_jobs\n      parameter. Multiple chunks processed in parallel, then aggregated.\n    evidence: daxgen.py uses ind_jobs to split threshold (line count) into step sizes.\n\n  - pattern_type: data_reuse_across_analysis_tasks\n    description: >\n      Single individuals_merged_tarball and sifted_file are reused by both\n      mutation_overlap and frequency tasks (no duplication).\n    evidence: Both tasks consume same data objects; pc_edges show 1-to-n fan-out.\n\n  - pattern_type: metadata_filtering_broadcast\n    description: >\n      Sifted file (SIFT filtering metadata) is broadcast to all population\n      analysis jobs to enable consistent filtering.\n    evidence: sifting->mutation_overlap and sifting->frequency edges are 1-to-n broadcasts.\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: io:tarball_compression_overhead\n    task_affected: [task:individuals, task:individuals_merge, task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    description: >\n      Significant compression/decompression overhead due to tar.gz format.\n      Every job using tarball inputs must extract before processing,\n      then recompress on output (except mutation_overlap/frequency which output tar format).\n    severity: moderate\n    optimization_hint: >\n      Consider keeping tarballs decompressed on shared filesystem if I/O bandwidth available.\n      Reduces CPU overhead of compression but increases storage footprint.\n\n  - hint_id: io:small_file_multiplication\n    task_affected: [task:individuals, task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    description: >\n      Individuals job creates ~2500 small files (one per individual per chromosome).\n      Mutation_overlap and frequency jobs read all these files repeatedly.\n      Small file I/O (stat, open, close) overhead is significant.\n    severity: moderate\n    optimization_hint: >\n      Batch small files into larger units or use memory-mapped access.\n      Current tar.gz approach is reasonable mitigation.\n\n  - hint_id: io:metadata_heavy_parsing\n    task_affected: [task:individuals, task:sifting, task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    description: >\n      VCF and VEP parsing involves extracting fields from tab-delimited text.\n      Multiple column splits and string manipulations per line.\n      Large files (gigabytes) with millions of lines amplify overhead.\n    severity: low\n    optimization_hint: >\n      Consider binary intermediate formats (HDF5, Parquet) for data passing\n      between tasks instead of VCF text.\n\n  - hint_id: io:format_consistency\n    task_affected: [task:individuals, task:individuals_merge, task:sifting, task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    description: >\n      Individual-level data format is text (per-individual text file in tarball).\n      Consistent format maintained throughout pipeline (no format conversions).\n    severity: low\n    notes: No format mismatch issues detected.\n\n  - hint_id: io:memory_resident_large_arrays\n    task_affected: [task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    description: >\n      Analysis tasks load entire per-individual mutation lists into memory\n      (Counter objects, numpy arrays). For large populations (2500+ individuals),\n      memory usage can be substantial during pairwise operations.\n    severity: moderate\n    optimization_hint: >\n      Implement streaming or chunked overlap computation to reduce memory footprint.\n      Current approach loads all data at once.\n\n  - hint_id: io:plotting_output_heavy\n    task_affected: [task:mutation_overlap, task:frequency]\n    description: >\n      Matplotlib PNG generation creates multiple plot files per population per chromosome.\n      Typical outputs: distribution plots, colormap heatmaps (rasterized images).\n      I/O for image files is sequential write; may create filesystem metadata bottleneck.\n    severity: low\n    optimization_hint: >\n      Consider vector graphics (SVG/PDF) or HDF5-based plot storage\n      for archival if storage efficiency is concern.\n\ncritical_data_dependencies:\n  - dependency: individuals_merged_tarball reused by mutation_overlap and frequency\n    reason: >\n      Both analysis tasks consume same tarball. Ensures consistency\n      between overlap and frequency analyses without reprocessing.\n    consequence: >\n      If individuals_merge job fails, both analysis jobs cannot proceed.\n      Requires individuals_merge success guarantee.\n\n  - dependency: sifted_file broadcast to all analysis tasks\n    reason: >\n      SIFT filtering applied consistently across all populations.\n      Ensures cross-population comparisons use same filter criteria.\n    consequence: >\n      If sifting fails, all population analysis jobs fail.\n      Sifting is critical path.\n\nassumptions:\n  - assumption_id: assume:chr_independence\n    description: >\n      Chromosomes are processed independently with no cross-chromosome dependencies.\n      Analysis results per chromosome are independent.\n    basis: >\n      Task definitions read/write chromosome-specific files (chrX naming).\n      No inter-chromosome data movement observed in daxgen.py.\n\n  - assumption_id: assume:population_stationarity\n    description: >\n      Population files (population lists) are static and do not change across runs.\n      Same population membership across all chromosomes.\n    basis: >\n      Population files stored in data/populations/ as static reference.\n      No population generation logic in workflow.\n\n  - assumption_id: assume:vcf_completeness\n    description: >\n      VCF input files are complete and well-formed (no partial or corrupted files).\n      All 2504 individuals present in genotype columns.\n    basis: >\n      VCF parsing assumes standard format. No error recovery for malformed files.\n\n  - assumption_id: assume:individuals_tarball_lifecycle\n    description: >\n      Individuals tarball generated by individuals job is transient intermediate.\n      Not reused beyond individuals_merge. Can be deleted after merge completes.\n    basis: >\n      Tarball lifecycle marked as intermediate_staging. No other tasks depend on it.\n\nworkflow_summary:\n  total_task_class